│ patch_name               │ symmetry_shared_two_angle                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the 24 independent parameters per block with two symmetry-shared angles: one      │
│                          │ collective RY angle and one collective RZ angle. The alternating collective rotations and │
│                          │ CZ chain remain expressive across six independently parameterized repetitions, while      │
│                          │ respecting the permutation-like symmetry induced by averaging Z-Z readouts. The           │
│                          │ interleaved RY layers change the measured basis, the RZ layers provide phase sensitivity  │
│                          │ before subsequent repetitions, and the CZ chain supplies nonlocal mixing. This reduces    │
│                          │ the circuit parameters from 144 to 12 and total parameters from 146 to 14, strongly       │
│                          │ improving parameter efficiency and reducing overfitting risk while preserving the         │
│                          │ successful structure of the current ansatz.                                               │
