│ patch_description        │ Replace the 24 independent angles per block with two collective angles shared across all  │
│                          │ eight qubits. The shared RY layer changes the measurement basis and directly exposes      │
│                          │ non-Z correlations, while the shared RZ layer between repeated RY layers supplies a       │
│                          │ second noncommuting control axis. The CZ chain retains entangling dynamics, making the    │
│                          │ six repetitions a compact QAOA-like circuit. This reduces the circuit parameters from 144 │
│                          │ to 12, and total trainable parameters from 146 to 14, while preserving a structure well   │
│                          │ suited to symmetric state-property classification and reducing overfitting risk.          │
