│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ shared_global_ry                                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the identity-equivalent CZ-only block with a symmetry-preserving global RY layer  │
│                          │ followed by a CZ chain. All eight RY gates share one parameter within each block, so the  │
│                          │ six repetitions introduce only six circuit parameters and eight total parameters          │
│                          │ including readout calibration. RY rotations directly transform the measured Z-Z           │
│                          │ observables, while the interleaved CZ chain makes later rotations generate correlated,    │
│                          │ nonlinear features. This retains much of the successful seed’s structure while sharply    │
│                          │ reducing its 146-parameter burden and avoiding RZ layers that are redundant when adjacent │
│                          │ to the Z-diagonal entanglers and readout.                                                 │
