│ patch_name               │ shared_global_layers                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the ineffective parameter-free CZ with a symmetry-preserving, parameter-efficient │
│                          │ hardware-efficient block. One shared RY parameter changes the measurement basis on every  │
│                          │ qubit, while one shared RZ parameter supplies a complementary noncommuting axis. A        │
│                          │ nearest-neighbor CZ chain between repetitions converts the six independent shared         │
│                          │ rotation pairs into an expressive QAOA-like sequence rather than a collapsible product of │
│                          │ rotations. Parameter sharing reduces the circuit from 146 total parameters to 14 (12      │
│                          │ circuit parameters plus gain and bias), which should retain much of the successful seed   │
│                          │ circuit’s expressivity while improving convergence, regularization, and parameter         │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
