│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ single_axis_collective                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Remove the collective RZ layer and retain the trainable collective RY rotations           │
│                          │ interleaved with the fixed CZ chain. Because each of the six repetitions has an           │
│                          │ independent copy of the shared block parameter, the circuit still learns a six-angle      │
│                          │ nonlinear sequence while reducing the total parameter count from 14 to 8. RZ rotations    │
│                          │ immediately before the next collective RY layer add phase flexibility but double the      │
│                          │ circuit parameters; the perfect accuracy of the symmetric current model suggests that the │
│                          │ lower-dimensional collective subspace captures the dataset structure. This ablation       │
│                          │ should improve parameter efficiency, reduce gate count and depth, and potentially         │
│                          │ accelerate convergence while preserving the entangling transformation needed to alter the │
│                          │ Z-Z readout.                                                                              │
