│ patch_description        │ Use a parameter-free identity-echo ansatz and let the dataset-aligned Z-Z readout perform │
│                          │ the classification directly. A single CZ is applied in each block; because the block      │
│                          │ repeats six times and CZ is self-inverse, the total ansatz is exactly the identity. This  │
│                          │ preserves the input correlators without unnecessary variational distortion while          │
│                          │ retaining only the required trainable gain and bias. The result reduces the model from 14 │
│                          │ to 2 trainable parameters, lowers gate count and depth, and should converge quickly when  │
│                          │ the fixed correlators already encode the target property.                                 │
