│ patch_name               │ tied_euler_collective                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses two independent collective angles per block, producing 12 circuit │
│                          │ parameters across 6 repeats plus gain and bias, for 14 total parameters. The proposed     │
│                          │ block ties the collective RY and RZ rotations to the same angle. This preserves           │
│                          │ noncommuting collective dynamics and the full CZ entangling line while reducing the model │
│                          │ to one circuit parameter per block: 6 circuit parameters and 2 readout parameters, or 8   │
│                          │ total. Adam’s learning rate (0.03), batch size (15), 30 steps per epoch, validation-loss  │
│                          │ early stopping, and six independent repetitions remain unchanged. The reduced search      │
│                          │ space should converge quickly, improve parameter efficiency from approximately 0.071 to   │
│                          │ 0.125 at perfect test accuracy, and regularize against unnecessary train-validation       │
│                          │ divergence.                                                                               │
