│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ identity_readout_only                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Reduce the circuit to a parameter-free identity transformation so the classifier directly │
│                          │ exploits the dataset-defined averaged Z-Z correlator. A single CZ is valid and, because   │
│                          │ the block is repeated six times, applies as CZ^6 = I. This removes all circuit angles,    │
│                          │ leaving only the gain and bias for two total trainable parameters. Since the current      │
│                          │ model already achieves perfect accuracy and the readout is evidently highly informative,  │
│                          │ this should substantially improve parameter efficiency, reduce depth and gate count, and  │
│                          │ accelerate convergence while retaining direct calibration of the raw correlator signal.   │
