│ patch_type               │ cross                                                                                     │
│ patch_name               │ collective_ry_floquet                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover retains the current program’s one-parameter-per-repeat economy while       │
│                          │ adopting the inspiration program’s independently meaningful collective RY structure. The  │
│                          │ tied RZ layer is removed because it constrains the same angle to two different rotation   │
│                          │ axes, and the final RZ layer also commutes with the Z-Z readout. The resulting block uses │
│                          │ six circuit parameters plus gain and bias (eight total), while reducing the circuit from  │
│                          │ 138 to 90 ansatz gates. Collective RY rotations provide the noncommuting trainable        │
│                          │ dynamics, and the fixed CZ chain propagates correlations across all qubits.               │
