│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ identity_calibrated_readout                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the trainable collective circuit with a single fixed CZ per block. Because the    │
│                          │ block is repeated six times, the identical CZ is applied an even number of times and      │
│                          │ cancels exactly, yielding an identity ansatz. This directly exposes the dataset-provided  │
│                          │ mean Z-Z feature to the trainable gain and bias. The prior results already show perfect   │
│                          │ classification near the identity initialization, suggesting that the fixed correlators    │
│                          │ carry the relevant signal. This reduces total trainable parameters from 8 to the          │
│                          │ theoretical minimum of 2, reduces gate count from 138 to 6, and avoids unnecessary        │
│                          │ circuit optimization while retaining calibration of the output scale and threshold.       │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
