│ patch_description        │ Remove the RZ rotations tied to the same angle as the RY layer. A shared angle across     │
│                          │ noncommuting RY and RZ gates constrains every repeat to an unnecessarily coupled rotation │
│                          │ axis, which can preserve classification accuracy while limiting L2 calibration quality. A │
│                          │ pure collective RY layer directly rotates the measured Z observables, while the CZ chain  │
│                          │ supplies fixed entangling structure. This retains the minimum achievable parameter count  │
│                          │ of one circuit parameter per repeat (8 total parameters including readout), reduces the   │
│                          │ gate count from 138 to 90, lowers circuit depth, and should provide a cleaner             │
│                          │ optimization landscape for improving validation loss without sacrificing the observed     │
│                          │ perfect accuracy.                                                                         │
