│ patch_name               │ readout_only_identity                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Remove all circuit parameters and retain a single fixed CZ as the required non-empty      │
│                          │ block. Because the block is repeated six times, CZ^6 is exactly the identity, so the      │
│                          │ classifier directly uses the dataset-provided mean Z-Z correlator with only the trainable │
│                          │ gain and bias. This reduces total parameters from 8 to 2, gate count from 138 to 6, and   │
│                          │ circuit depth substantially. The existing perfect accuracy and rapid convergence indicate │
│                          │ that the fixed correlator readout already contains the class signal; eliminating          │
│                          │ unnecessary rotations should improve parameter efficiency, simulation speed, and          │
│                          │ resistance to overfitting.                                                                │
