│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ identity_readout_only                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Collapse the variational circuit to a parameter-free identity over the six fixed          │
│                          │ repetitions. A single CZ is self-inverse, so applying the block six times gives CZ^6 = I  │
│                          │ exactly. This tests the strong inductive bias already suggested by near-perfect           │
│                          │ convergence from near-zero rotations: the dataset-provided averaged ZZ readout may itself │
│                          │ contain the classification signal. The candidate then trains only gain and bias, reducing │
│                          │ total parameters from 8 to 2, increasing parameter efficiency from 0.125 to as much as    │
│                          │ 0.5 at perfect accuracy, and sharply reducing gate count and depth. Eliminating circuit   │
│                          │ parameters also removes seed-dependent circuit optimization and overfitting risk.         │
