│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ identity_readout_calibrator                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses one independent collective angle in each of six repetitions, plus │
│                          │ gain and bias, for eight trainable parameters. Since it already achieves perfect          │
│                          │ classification, the primary opportunity is parameter economy, lower depth, and faster     │
│                          │ convergence rather than additional expressivity.                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed block contains only one fixed CZ gate. Because the identical block is        │
│                          │ repeated six times and CZ is self-inverse, the six applications cancel exactly. The       │
│                          │ resulting classifier operates directly on the dataset-provided mean ZZ feature and trains │
│                          │ only its gain and bias. This reduces the model from 8 to 2 trainable parameters, gate     │
│                          │ count from 138 to 6, and depth from 29 to 6. It also removes unnecessary circuit          │
│                          │ optimization and should improve parameter efficiency and convergence while preserving the │
│                          │ fixed training loop, measurements, block count, inputs, and outputs.                      │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
