│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ identity_probe                                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the trainable Floquet circuit with a parameter-free block containing one CZ gate. │
│                          │ Because the block is repeated exactly six times and CZ is self-inverse, the total ansatz  │
│                          │ is CZ^6 = I, so the measured dataset correlators are preserved exactly. Only the gain and │
│                          │ bias remain trainable, reducing the model from 8 to 2 parameters while also cutting gate  │
│                          │ count and depth substantially. Since the existing model already achieves perfect accuracy │
│                          │ and begins near the identity, this tests whether the fixed correlator mean already        │
│                          │ contains the classification signal and should maximize parameter efficiency and           │
│                          │ convergence speed without introducing an additional generalization gap.                   │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
