│ patch_name               │ identity_readout_only                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Collapse the variational circuit to an exact identity and train only the gain and bias. A │
│                          │ single CZ is self-inverse, and the fixed six repetitions apply it an even number of       │
│                          │ times, so the net ansatz is exactly identity. This directly exposes the dataset-provided  │
│                          │ averaged Z-Z correlators, which already appear sufficient for perfect classification,     │
│                          │ while reducing the total trainable parameter count from 8 to the theoretical minimum of 2 │
│                          │ readout parameters. It also reduces the gate count from 138 to 6 and avoids               │
│                          │ circuit-parameter optimization noise, potentially improving convergence and parameter     │
│                          │ efficiency substantially.                                                                 │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0390                                                                                   │
