│ patch_description        │ The current ansatz uses one shared angle per block, producing 6 circuit parameters plus   │
│                          │ the gain and bias. Although it reaches perfect accuracy, its validation/test L2 losses    │
│                          │ remain around 0.03/0.02 and it carries 8 trainable parameters.                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The proposed block contains only a fixed CZ gate. Since CZ commutes with every fixed Z-Z  │
│                          │ readout observable—and six identical repetitions also compose to the identity—this        │
│                          │ preserves the dataset’s native correlator signal without unnecessary trainable            │
│                          │ transformations. The model therefore trains only the readout gain and bias, reducing the  │
│                          │ total parameter count from 8 to 2, increasing parameter efficiency, reducing circuit      │
│                          │ depth and gate count, and avoiding noisy or redundant circuit-parameter optimization. The │
│                          │ fixed Adam settings remain learning rate 0.03, 30 steps per epoch, batch size 15,         │
│                          │ convergence threshold 0.90, and validation-loss early stopping with patience 75 and       │
│                          │ minimum improvement 1e-4.                                                                 │
