│ patch_description        │ Remove the tied collective RZ layer and retain one shared RY angle per repetition. The    │
│                          │ current RZ rotations are forced to use the same angle as the feature-changing RY          │
│                          │ rotations, imposing an unnecessary axis constraint; moreover, Z rotations and CZ gates    │
│                          │ commute with the Z-diagonal readout and can add optimization complexity without directly  │
│                          │ improving the measured correlators. This preserves the economy of one circuit parameter   │
│                          │ per block and eight total trainable parameters, while reducing the circuit from 138 to 90 │
│                          │ gates and giving each learned angle a clearer role. The simpler collective-RY/CZ dynamics │
│                          │ should improve convergence and L2 loss while maintaining the observed perfect             │
│                          │ classification accuracy.                                                                  │
